$ signet dev --help
-- stdout --
Develop a contract against a fork of its deployed version: build it, run
its saved calls on the deployed and the new code from the same forked state,
and compare, every time the source changes.

The contract, --path and --package come from the flags or, for what the flags
leave out, from the nearest signet.dev.toml (walking up from the working
directory); signet dev init writes one. Before anything starts, signet dev
checks, in order and each with its own message: the stellar CLI, cargo, the
wasm32v1-none Rust target, a contract (cdylib) crate at --path, the
signet-simulator, and that the simulator runs the network's protocol (exit 11
when it does not; exit 3 for the others).

--ci builds once, runs every check and exits with a code a pipeline can
branch on: 0 clean, 10 a difference in a --fail-on class (or a missed
expect), 12 a build failure, 6 or 7 a network problem or timeout, 11 an
unsupported protocol, 13 a simulator failure. --report writes a JSON report
(sandbox/protocol/schema/v1/ci-report.json) and --junit a JUnit file with
one testcase per replay, interface change and layout finding. With --bundle
the checks run offline, on a repro bundle's state and calls (signet sandbox
export), instead of a live fork.

Usage:
  signet dev [contract] [flags]
  signet dev [command]

Examples:
  signet dev CASFJHI5PQSRWS7JV25CF7FOMRKIVBP3RXRP3E2GH2CV4BCAG7FUJRCN --path ./contracts/registry
  signet dev            # everything from signet.dev.toml
  signet dev init CASF…RCN --path ./contracts/registry
  signet dev --ci --report report.json --junit junit.xml --fail-on breaking,spec

Available Commands:
  init        Write a signet.dev.toml for a deployed contract

Flags:
      --bundle string               with --ci, run offline on this repro bundle's state and calls instead of a live fork
      --ci                          run once, non-interactively, and exit 0 (clean), 10 (a --fail-on difference) or 12 (a failed build)
      --clear                       clear the screen before each cycle (on a terminal)
      --debounce duration           how long a burst of file changes must settle before one rebuild (default 150ms)
      --drift string                when an entry fetched for the fork changed on-chain after the fork ledger: warn, fail (exit 6), or refork (pin the latest ledger and run once more) (default "warn")
      --fail-on string              with --ci, what exits 10: breaking, behavioural, cost (replay differences), spec, layout (default "breaking,spec,layout")
  -h, --help                        help for dev
      --junit string                with --ci, write a JUnit XML file here
      --network-passphrase string   passphrase of a custom --network (checked against the RPC's getNetwork)
      --no-browser                  with --ui, print the UI's URL instead of opening a browser
      --package string              the contract crate, when --path is a workspace with several (default: package in signet.dev.toml)
      --path string                 the contract's crate directory (default: path in signet.dev.toml)
      --report string               with --ci, write a JSON report here
      --rpc-url string              Stellar RPC to fork from (overrides the context's rpc-url; testnet defaults to https://soroban-testnet.stellar.org)
      --scan-ledgers uint32         also scan the newest N ledgers for the contract's transactions that emitted no event (slow: every transaction in them is decoded)
      --timings string              json: also write each cycle's time by phase (and the start's) to stderr, one JSON object per line
      --ui                          also serve the local UI on 127.0.0.1 and open it
      --verbose                     print every difference of every replay (storage, events, the auth tree, resources) and the time by phase

Global Flags:
      --context string         deployment context to use (overrides SIGNET_CONTEXT and the config file's current context)
      --insecure               allow a plain-http deployment URL on a non-local host (signed challenges travel in cleartext; use only against a deployment you control)
      --json                   write a single JSON result to stdout instead of human-readable output (diagnostics go to stderr)
      --network string         Stellar network to talk to (overrides SIGNET_NETWORK, the context, and default "testnet")
      --sign-with-key string   identity to sign with, for non-interactive use (same value as STELLAR_SIGN_WITH_KEY; not remembered)
      --source string          identity to sign as (remembered in the config file for next time)
      --url string             Signet deployment URL (overrides SIGNET_URL, the config file, and the default)

Use "signet dev [command] --help" for more information about a command.
